2.2.1Ensure 'Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller' is set to 'No One

gpedit.msc

Navigate to Computer Configuration > Windows Settings > Security Settings > Local Policies > User Rights Assignment


regedit.exe

Computer\HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\PolicyManager\default\UserRights\AccessCredentialManagerAsTrustedCaller

Get-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\PolicyManager\default\UserRights\AccessCredentialManagerAsTrustedCaller" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\PolicyManager\default\UserRights\AccessCredentialManagerAsTrustedCaller"

$inf="$env:TEMP\user_rights.inf"; secedit /export /areas user_rights /cfg $inf /quiet | Out-Null; Get-Content $inf | Select-String "SeTrustedCredManAccessPrivilege"; Remove-Item $inf


